Change-Id: qlnvvlskllkmtxrsqnmyrztkxvrrkvyq

Nothing tells the operator whether lab-mail works short of sending
and fetching mail, and when it does not, which part failed. smtprelay
can be down while Dovecot keeps serving old mail, and a fetch that
stopped looks the same as a quiet list.

just check runs, from beastie, one check per part of the setup: the
jail, the credentials and who can read them, the mail state owners,
each service and its port, the age of the last successful fetch, and
the log files. Each prints ok or FAIL, and the exit status is 0 only
if all pass, so a script can act on it without parsing the output.

The fetch job now touches a file after each successful pull. Its age
shows that fetching works even when no mail arrives.
